 "title": "Parcel Search V2",
 "text": "Parcel Search V2\nParcel Search V2\nParcel Search By Dickinson County KS GIS\nOpen in a new window\n[ DKCOKS.Gov ] [ Appraisal Information Search ] [ Tax Information Search ] [ State Hosted Parcel Search App ]\nMeasure\nSelect\nMail List\nLayers\nImagery\nBookmark\nLegend\nPrint\nSearch in\nMove the cursor to get the coordinates\nSelect the output coordinate system\nEarthstar Geographics | Dickinson County GIS - Contact: Ricky Sekulich, Dickinson County GIS, gis@dickinsoncountyks.gov\nPowered by Esri\nSelect a sheet to display Road Lines\nActions\nTotal: 0 | Selection: 0\nWelcome to the DKCOKS Parcel Search Website\n[Disclaimer - Scroll For Full Text]\nThis dataset is provided by Dickinson County, Kansas for informational purposes only. Data are provided “as is” without warranty of any kind, expressed or implied, including but not limited to warranties of accuracy, completeness, timeliness, merchantability, or fitness for a particular purpose. Dickinson County assumes no liability for any direct, indirect, incidental, consequential, or special damages arising from use of the data.\nThis data is not a survey and shall not be used to determine precise boundaries, property lines, road centerlines, legal descriptions, or other authoritative determinations.\nPermitted use: You may view, download, and use this data for lawful purposes.\nAttribution: Please credit “Dickinson County, Kansas (GIS)” and include the date accessed.\nUse of lists of names and addresses derived from public records for certain solicitation purposes may be restricted under K.S.A. 45-220(c)(2) and K.S.A. 45-230.\nBy accessing the data herein, you certify that you agree to the above.\n[End of Disclaimer]\n[Update - 9 May 2025]\nAdded a new information layer called \"Named Locations\" to provide a convenient way to familiarize and orientate yourself to the area you're viewing.\nThis layer is off by default but is just a few clicks away in the toolbar section labeled \"Layers\" simply check the box to turn it on and off.\nWhile we have made effort to ensure accuracy, some locations may still need updates. We welcome community input and insights. If you notice discrepancies, please share your observations with us at [ gis@dkcoks.gov ] to help us maintain the quality and relevance of our data.\"\nI agree to the above\nOK",
